0.43	One sound heard as two (German “dauert” said with an [r] and a vowel) is drawn as one column, and costs what the host's table says. A sound the check finds likely off costs at least the host's floor.
0.42	One warning, not two: a sound the picture already shows as different (with its box) gets no warning line as well; a line is written only where the picture shows the sound as right.
0.41	A take that was not understood shows the sounds as the recogniser heard them; only an understood take shows them checked against the sound check.
0.40	What counts as heard: a sound heard differently, or left out, counts only where the sound check flagged it; elsewhere the target's sound is taken. A variant that costs nothing is shown as the target's sound. Sounds the recogniser cannot judge are marked “not judged”.
0.39	One session per learner: a name signed in on another screen is marked so in the list, and signing in as it is refused, with the reason. With a form open, Sign out and a change of the language practised wait until it is saved or cancelled, so no typed change is lost. (The lock of 0.38 is gone: it guarded two sessions of one learner, which can no longer happen.)
0.38	A word whose form is open in your other session is locked here: its row says it is being edited in your other session, and Edit, its note and Delete are greyed until that form is closed (Cancel, Save, a change of language or sign-out there).
0.37	The result is one picture: each word with its target sounds and the sounds heard beneath, coloured by how close they are. The words heard are written as the phrase writes them.
0.36	The choosers of lists offer only lists of the language you practise; Load says which language the list is kept under.
0.35	Two sessions stand side by side on a wide window.
0.34	A long vowel no longer runs into the next sound in the lines of sounds.
0.33	Continue as a guest: the whole app, and nothing is kept.
0.32	Sign in, register and sign out. Your settings are saved when you sign out.
0.31	The settings are a view of their own: Settings opens it, Done returns to the app as you left it.
0.30	Your practice list is kept for each language: a change of language, or a restart, shows it again with no import. Lists of words to choose from in Upload (where the host provides them).
0.29	The recording held, its Play it button and its picture stand in one row on a wide screen.
0.28	The recording held can be played and is shown (where the host provides it).
0.27	Go to any phrase: each line of “The list” is a button.
0.26	Warnings, not errors: the marks are on the sounds heard, in one colour (dotted: worth a listen; solid: likely off); a line says what the percentage measures.
0.25	A phrase file is phrase, a tab, meaning (or phrase | meaning): a comma no longer splits a line.
0.24	The result compares sound by sound, the heard sounds under the target's; the heard sounds are shown word by word even when the recogniser gives no word breaks.
0.23	The version beside the title; a file can fill the Load and Upload boxes; nothing else can be pressed while a recording is being made.
0.22	Ready for a real host: Hear it, the host's lists, a recorder area (shown only when the host provides them); a flag line names its word only when it can.
0.21	Version line in the foot (what this page is, which engine, what is new); the test host keeps what is stored across restarts.
0.20	Runs on any host of the engine; test controls only on a test host.
0.19	A tap on an inactive button says why.
0.18	An inactive control says why; a step says what it did.
0.17	Every button is active only when its press would do something.
0.16	Record and Load say a status message each time.
